@startuml
title EKA-13 selected fix — isolate and make Docker access read-only
participant "Monitor" as Monitor
participant "private internal\nnetwork" as Private
participant "docker-proxy\nv0.4.2@digest\nPOST=0" as Proxy
database "Host Docker daemon" as Docker
participant "Other net_ekklesia peer" as Peer

Monitor -> Monitor : AUTO_RECOVERY_T2=false; escalate to T3
Monitor -> Private : sole consumer
Private -> Proxy : permitted read path
Peer -[#red,dashed]> Proxy : no shared network route
Proxy -> Docker : Docker API via mounted socket
Proxy -[#red,dashed]> Docker : POST denied
Proxy -> Docker : no enabled API namespace

note over Proxy
Dedicated internal network closes lateral peer access.
POST=0 removes restart writes.
Container/event/ping/version GETs and all Docker writes are denied while T2 is disabled.
end note
@enduml
